tance snapshot's recorded `cwd`, the directory the first start spawned its child in. It reads that value only after the strict-modes check on the instance's files, and it must name an existing directory, else the revive is refused `cwd-missing`. Program resolution and the version gate never read the recorded directory: the program is looked up on the reviving process's own `PATH`, from its own current directory (a boundary widening the founder ratified live on 2026-10-10, after it was shown to him as one, the overseer and the operator as relay; chunk 2026-10-10-viola-revive). viola resolves the child program to an absolute path itself (portable-pty's Windows search tries the exact name first and hits the extensionless npm sh shim). The pump keeps the ConPTY input writer until the child exits, because dropping it makes conhost send `CTRL_CLOSE` to the child (exit `0xC000013A`). The exit is recorded as `exit_source` `handle-wait` or `kill-fallback`. As measured (chunk 2026-09-29-h2-conpty-resize-probe, H2): a key written through the seam right after `resize` returned can fail to reach the child — on the windows-2025 runner (image `windows-2025-vs2026` 20260922.246.2), in an isolated loop of the viola-pty red test under `cargo llvm-cov nextest`, 13 of 200 iterations lost it (ci#36527891850), every loss the same class: the child's key-free size watcher saw the new size, viola's writer wrote and flushed the key, and the Rust test child blocked in its console read never received it; ConPTY wrote no cursor-position request (`dsr-cpr 0` on every loss, and on the dev host, Windows 10.0.26200.9457 / conhost 10.0.26100.8875, which read 20/20). The measured span runs from the ConPTY input-pipe write to that test child's console read; where inside it the key is lost is not established (an overseer read of microsoft/terminal's current source, relayed at that chunk's wrap, found no input-buffer flush on the resize path — a relay, not verified here). Whether the real `claude` (Node